Optimal Solution - Dynamic programming solution to compute the longest common subsequence between two strings.
                   Define DP on prefixes of both strings and build the answer by matching or skipping characters optimally.

class Solution {
    public int longestCommonSubsequence(String text1, String text2) {
        // dp[i][j] represents the LCS length of
        // text1[0..i-1] and text2[0..j-1]
        int dp[][] = new int[text1.length() + 1][text2.length() + 1];
        // Build the DP table bottom-up
        for (int i = 1; i <= text1.length(); i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= text2.length(); j++) {
                // If current characters match, extend LCS
                if (text1.charAt(i - 1) == text2.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                }
                // Otherwise, take the maximum by skipping one character
                else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
                }
            }
        }
        // LCS length is stored in the last cell
        return dp[text1.length()][text2.length()];
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n x m).
Space Complexity :- O(n x m).
